          "lessonId": "p1-b2-l03",
          "reminder": "Divisibility depends on the full coefficient, including prime factors supplied by the combination number."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p>The coefficient is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00029;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></math>. For every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></math>, the powers already contain <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></math>, the coefficient <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> is also divisible by 12. At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>, it is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>, which lacks a factor 3; at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math>, it is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>, which is odd.</p><p>Exactly the 11 indices <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>&#x02026;</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></math> work: <strong>E.</strong></p>",
